# Solaar (Logitech device manager, in the image) creates a virtual keyboard
# "solaar-keyboard" through uinput as soon as it starts, for its key-remapping
# rules. GNOME takes it for an attached hardware keyboard and leaves touch
# mode: the on-screen keyboard no longer opens (also not on the lock screen)
# and the auto-rotate button disappears from the quick settings.
# Hidden from libinput, so the desktop never sees it. Solaar's settings,
# battery display and pairing are not affected; only its rules that type keys
# stop having an effect.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="solaar-keyboard", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
